// ExactMeshBoolean.open_winding_per_patch (L1 of the tail case): per patch, the first piece's Antipodal evaluation and the bound of the variation
[assembly: SuppressMessage("Reliability", "G3E0002", Scope = "member", Target = "~M:g3.ExactMeshBoolean.open_winding_per_patch(System.Collections.Generic.List{System.Int32},System.Collections.Generic.List{System.Int32}[],System.Collections.Generic.List{System.Int32},System.Int32[],System.Boolean[],System.Collections.Generic.List{System.Int64})~g3.ExactMeshBoolean.PatchOpen", Justification = "reviewed: one patch per item: its first piece's evaluation into its own slot (Value), a serial Dijkstra over its own pieces (a heap and sums per worker, PatchSearch) into their own flags (Decided); the adjacency and the boundary data built serially before the loop and only read; integer counts by Interlocked; no floating-point reduction across threads")]

// ExactMeshBoolean.trace_open_winding (L2 of the tail case, T5 clusters): per cluster of adjacent input triangles, its pieces traced serially from a reference with exact crossing counts
[assembly: SuppressMessage("Reliability", "G3E0002", Scope = "member", Target = "~M:g3.ExactMeshBoolean.trace_open_winding(System.Collections.Generic.List{System.Int32},System.Collections.Generic.List{System.Int32}[],System.Boolean[],g3.ExactMeshBoolean.PatchOpen)~g3.ExactMeshBoolean.Traced", Justification = "reviewed: one cluster of input triangles per item (formed serially before the loop, each piece in one cluster, its local index written before the loop), its pieces traced serially in a fixed order into their own slots (Value, Has); integer crossing counts, each boundary sum within one piece; the boundary and far-point data only read; the far-point projections of the boundary segments built once per far point by CompareExchange (a deterministic function of the read-only data, the first stored kept); integer counts by Interlocked, the verify margins under a lock (tests only); no floating-point reduction across threads")]

// ExactMeshBoolean.classify: per-piece coplanar stacks, the coplanar walk (one task per walked source, its own slice of the stack and representative arrays), per-patch winding numbers (thread-local candidate lists)
[assembly: SuppressMessage("Reliability", "G3E0002", Scope = "member", Target = "~M:g3.ExactMeshBoolean.classify(System.Boolean[]@,System.Boolean[]@)", Justification = "reviewed: per-piece and per-patch writes, the coplanar walk (#1630: one task per walked source writes only the slices of the stack and representative arrays of its own pieces, reads the edge planes of its source, which the arrangement fixed before, and calls the same coplanar_stack, centroid / AddPoint and inside_coplanar as the per-piece loop; its only shared value is the Interlocked test counter, which feeds Counts and no decision), integer winding numbers (the open meshes' generalized ones, by fast winding numbers or by the Antipodal Method's exact ray and boundary sum, each summed within its own piece in a fixed order, thresholded per piece), no floating-point reduction across threads; the boundary segments and boxes of the Antipodal meshes computed serially before the loop, the fast-winding trees of the other open meshes one per task and stored serially afterwards; the loop only reads them")]

// ContouringTopologyCertificate.Cells: per-chunk workers with their own marks and tables over read-only shared arrays (L,
// the bins, the grid); each writes the reasons of its own cell indices. No floating-point value crosses threads: a cell's
// reason is a function of the geometry of the cell, its faces and their edges alone (the exact tests on the triangles of L
// that meet them), so faces and edges tested twice on chunk borders give the same records; the integer test counters are
// summed serially in chunk order (diagnostic counts: border faces and edges are counted twice, so they depend on the
// chunking; the reasons do not). Parallel equals serial bit for bit (ContouringTopologyCertificateTests, WindingContouringCertificateTests)
[assembly: SuppressMessage("Reliability", "G3E0002", Scope = "member", Target = "~M:g3.ContouringTopologyCertificate.Cells(System.Collections.Generic.IList{System.Collections.Generic.KeyValuePair{g3.Vector3i,System.Int32}},System.Collections.Generic.IList{System.Boolean},System.Boolean,System.Int32)~g3.ContouringCertificateReason[]", Justification = "reviewed: per-chunk workers, per-index writes, no floating-point reduction")]
